<header><h1>The Ghosts of Creuss: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_creuss">The Ghosts of Creuss</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="quantum-entanglement"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Quantum%20Entanglement">Quantum Entanglement</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The effect of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Enforced%20Travel%20Ban"><i>Enforced Travel Ban</i></a> law does not affect the Creuss player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What exactly does Creuss&rsquo;s Quantum Entanglement connect &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;no game effect, Enforced Travel Ban included, can stop that.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Creuss player has units or controls planets in a system with an alpha wormhole, and another player has units or controls planets in a system with a beta wormhole, or vice versa, then the Creuss player and that player are neighbors.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Mentak Coalition use the &lsquo;Pillage&rsquo; faction ability &hellip; when they are neighbors with another faction as a result of &hellip; &lsquo;Quantum Entanglement&rsquo; faction ability? A: Yes, even in the case of &lsquo;Quantum Entanglement&rsquo; only being active from the Creuss&rsquo; point of view, because the &lsquo;neighbor&rsquo; status is active as a result of the ability.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 101.3: &ldquo;Players can be neighbors and perform transactions through wormholes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Are the Ghosts of Creuss neighbors with a player on a beta wormhole when Creuss sits on an alpha wormhole?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; Quantum Entanglement makes alpha and beta wormholes adjacent for Creuss, and adjacency created that way also makes them neighbors, so the two players can transact.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player may use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> ability against the Creuss player in this manner.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;because the &lsquo;neighbor&rsquo; status is active as a result of the ability, the Mentak may use their &lsquo;Pillage&rsquo; in these situations.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If <a href="/R_mecatol_rex">Mecatol Rex</a> contains an alpha wormhole, then the &ldquo;For&rdquo; effect of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Ixthian%20Artifact"><i>Ixthian Artifact</i></a> agenda will not affect the Creuss player&rsquo;s units in a system with a beta wormhole (and no alpha wormhole), and vice versa.<sup>1,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;If there is an &lsquo;A&rsquo; wormhole on Mecatol Rex when the &lsquo;Ixthian Artifact&rsquo; agenda causes units in adjacent systems to be destroyed, does the Quantum Entanglement ability cause the Ghost of Creuss faction to lose units in a system that contains a &lsquo;B&rsquo; wormhole? A: No. Only the Creuss treats those systems as adjacent.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (sigmazero13, Sep 11, 2018): &ldquo;The intent is that it would not work that way.&rdquo; Alpha at Mecatol does not affect Creuss ships in a beta system; vice versa by symmetry.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Other players cannot use <sc>Quantum Entanglement</sc> to produce hits from a unit with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/PDS#Upgraded_Unit:~:text=Deep%20Space%20Cannon"><sc>Deep Space Cannon</sc></a> ability against the Creuss player&rsquo;s units.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What exactly does Creuss&rsquo;s Quantum Entanglement connect &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Other players can&rsquo;t fire Space Cannon or move through that connection.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="slipstream"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Slipstream">Slipstream</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Enforced%20Travel%20Ban"><i>Enforced Travel Ban</i></a> law has no effect on <sc>Slipstream</sc>.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Enforced Travel Ban stop Creuss&rsquo;s Slipstream bonus?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; Slipstream only checks for a wormhole in the ship&rsquo;s starting system.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Enforced Travel Ban has no effect on Slipstream.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><sc>Slipstream</sc> does not apply to the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Creuss%20Gate">Creuss Gate</a> or to the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Flagship:~:text=Hil%20Colish"><i>Hil Colish</i></a>, or to gamma wormholes.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="creuss-gate"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Creuss%20Gate">Creuss Gate</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A frontier token is placed in the Creuss Gate system during setup.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 38 (Frontier Tokens), d: &ldquo;A frontier token is placed in the Creuss gate system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Creuss home system (in standard game board setups) is on the edge of the board.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook p. 16: &ldquo;The wormhole nexus and the Ghosts of Creuss&rsquo; home system are on the edge of the game board for the purpose of scoring objectives.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 39.2a: &ldquo;The Ghosts of Creuss home system and the wormhole nexus are on the edge of the game board.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="creuss-iff"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Creuss%20IFF">Creuss IFF</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player may receive the <i>Creuss IFF</i> in a transaction during their turn. If received at the start of that player&rsquo;s turn, that player may play it immediately.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;a promissory note with &lsquo;At the start of your turn:&rsquo; timing may be immediately played if the transaction occurred&rdquo; in that window.</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I receive Creuss IFF in a transaction at the start of my turn and play it in that same window?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; it is still the start of your turn until you actually take an action.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;You can trade a promissory note and have it be immediately used during the start of turn window. That is allowed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The <i>Creuss IFF</i> cannot be played twice in one timing window.<sup>1,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 1.18: &ldquo;Each ability can be resolved once for each occurrence of that ability&rsquo;s timing event.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;because of rule 1.16, that PN cannot be traded and resolved multiple times during the same window.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Any deal between the Creuss player and another player regarding where the wormhole tokens will be placed, if made before the <i>Creuss IFF</i> is exchanged, is non&ndash;binding.<sup>1,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling, on a deal to trade the Creuss IFF and have it used: &ldquo;This would be non-binding, because when the deal is made, the non-Ghost player does not technically qualify to even be able to perform his side of the deal (he doesn&rsquo;t have the IFF).&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 28.4: &ldquo;If the terms of a deal cannot be resolved immediately, it is a non-binding deal.&rdquo; placement occurs later than the deal, so it cannot be resolved immediately.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Creuss IFF</i> may be played even if the Creuss player has not researched <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Wormhole%20Generator"><i>Wormhole Generator</i></a>.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Creuss Promissory note still be used if the Creuss have not researched &lsquo;Wormhole Generator&rsquo;? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Creuss IFF</i> cannot place wormhole tokens in the home system of an eliminated player, unless the player resolving it controls a planet in that system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Creuss IFF note put a wormhole token in a system with enemy ships if I control a planet there?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the two placement options are alternatives: a system containing a planet you control, or a non-home system with no other players&rsquo; ships. Meeting either is enough&rdquo; An eliminated player&rsquo;s home system is still a home system, so only the planet-control option allows it.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Creuss IFF</i> may place wormhole tokens in <a href="/R_fracture">The Fracture</a>.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Wormhole Generator (Technology): Can wormholes be placed in The Fracture? Also applies to placing wormholes with Creuss IFF. A: Yes, wormholes can be placed in the Fracture.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="dimensional-splicer"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Dimensional%20Splicer">Dimensional Splicer</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any wormhole may trigger <i>Dimensional Splicer</i>, including the one produced by the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Flagship:~:text=Hil%20Colish"><i>Hil Colish</i></a>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Creuss flagship&rsquo;s delta wormhole trigger Dimensional Splicer?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; it is a wormhole.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>One hit will be produced even if the system contains multiple wormholes.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Creuss player chooses which ship the hit is assigned to.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When Dimensional Splicer or Yin&rsquo;s Devotion hits my ship, who picks the target &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Creuss or Yin player chooses which of your ships takes the hit.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Shields%20Holding"><i>Shields Holding</i></a> action card may be used to cancel the hit.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;&rsquo;Shields Holding&rsquo; may be used to cancel hits that are produced by these abilities,&rdquo; including &ldquo;Dimensional Splicer.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Direct Hit and Shields Holding work on hits from Dimensional Splicer or Yin Devotion?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes to both.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The chosen ship may cancel the hit by using its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, if present. A different ship with the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability cannot do so.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When Dimensional Splicer or Yin&rsquo;s Devotion hits my ship &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Only that ship can use its own Sustain Damage to cancel it; you can&rsquo;t move the hit elsewhere.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the chosen ship cancels the hit by using its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card may be used.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;&rsquo;Direct Hit&rsquo; can be used to follow up hits that are assigned by &lsquo;Ambush,&rsquo; &lsquo;Dimensional Splicer,&rsquo; &lsquo;Devotion,&rsquo; and other similar abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Creuss flagship&rsquo;s delta wormhole trigger Dimensional Splicer?&rdquo;: &ldquo;which can set up Direct Hit.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: Direct Hits target &ldquo;different ships/instances of sustain damage use.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="wormhole-generator" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Wormhole%20Generator">Wormhole Generator</a> (replaced by &Omega;) <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega; version.<sup>10</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>10</sup> Codex I p. 8, &ldquo;The Omega Initiative&rdquo;: &ldquo;Components from this section replace preexisting components of the same name and type.&rdquo; The Omega Initiative contents (p. 3) list &ldquo;Wormhole Generator&rdquo;.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>This ability is mandatory for the Creuss player in every status phase after it has been researched.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is Creuss&rsquo;s Wormhole Generator mandatory &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A player relays a developer email saying it is mandatory each status phase, since it lacks &lsquo;may&rsquo;.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Sep 2017): &ldquo;The effect is mandatory, once researched.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Creuss player may move a wormhole token from the system it is in into the same system.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;there is nothing stopping the Creuss from &lsquo;moving&rsquo; the token into the system that it is already in.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li><i>Wormhole Generator</i> cannot place wormhole tokens in the home system of an eliminated player, unless the Creuss player controls a planet in that system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Creuss IFF note put a wormhole token in a system with enemy ships if I control a planet there?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the two placement options are alternatives: a system containing a planet you control, or a non-home system with no other players&rsquo; ships. Meeting either is enough&rdquo; Wormhole Generator uses the same two placement options as the Creuss IFF, and an eliminated player&rsquo;s home system is still a home system, so only the planet-control option allows it.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Creuss wormhole tokens may be placed in <a href="/R_fracture">The Fracture</a>.<sup>2,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Wormhole Generator (Technology): Can wormholes be placed in The Fracture? Also applies to placing wormholes with Creuss IFF. A: Yes, wormholes can be placed in the Fracture.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do empty Fracture systems get frontier tokens, and can wormholes go there?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Wormholes can be placed there, since nothing forbids it.&rdquo; wormhole tokens may be placed in Fracture systems.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Neutral ships prevent a Creuss wormhole token from being placed in their system, in the same way as another player&rsquo;s ships.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, &ldquo;Do neutral ships block wormhole placement?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Do neutral ships block wormhole placement? A: Yes&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Creuss player may use <i>Wormhole Generator</i> to place a wormhole token in an entropic scar; the card is exhausted and the token is then discarded.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can Creuss use Wormhole Generator when an entropic scar is present to remove a wormhole token &hellip;? A: Yes, Wormhole Generator will exhaust and place a token, which will then be discarded.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="wormhole-generator-omega"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Wormhole%20Generator">Wormhole Generator &Omega;</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Wormhole Generator &Omega;</i> cannot place wormhole tokens in the home system of an eliminated player, unless the Creuss player controls a planet in that system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Creuss IFF note put a wormhole token in a system with enemy ships if I control a planet there?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the two placement options are alternatives: a system containing a planet you control, or a non-home system with no other players&rsquo; ships. Meeting either is enough&rdquo; Wormhole Generator uses the same two placement options as the Creuss IFF, and an eliminated player&rsquo;s home system is still a home system, so only the planet-control option allows it.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Creuss wormhole tokens may be placed in <a href="/R_fracture">The Fracture</a>.<sup>2,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Wormhole Generator (Technology): Can wormholes be placed in The Fracture? Also applies to placing wormholes with Creuss IFF. A: Yes, wormholes can be placed in the Fracture.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do empty Fracture systems get frontier tokens, and can wormholes go there?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Wormholes can be placed there, since nothing forbids it.&rdquo; wormhole tokens may be placed in Fracture systems.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Neutral ships prevent a Creuss wormhole token from being placed in their system, in the same way as another player&rsquo;s ships.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, &ldquo;Do neutral ships block wormhole placement?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Do neutral ships block wormhole placement? A: Yes&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Creuss player may use <i>Wormhole Generator &Omega;</i> to place a wormhole token in an entropic scar; the card is exhausted and the token is then discarded.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can Creuss use Wormhole Generator when an entropic scar is present to remove a wormhole token &hellip;? A: Yes, Wormhole Generator will exhaust and place a token, which will then be discarded.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="hil-colish"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Flagship:~:text=Hil%20Colish">Hil Colish</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the <i>Hil Colish</i> moves first, then the Creuss player uses the new position of the <i>Hil Colish</i> when determining if the active system may be reached by their other ships.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Creuss flagship&rsquo;s &lsquo;move before or after your other ships&rsquo; work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;If it moves into the active system first, that system becomes adjacent to other delta wormholes such as the Creuss home system, so your other ships can come in through it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <i>Hil Colish</i> moves last, then it may move itself into (or through, if its move value is increased) the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Creuss%20Gate">Creuss Gate</a> or Creuss home system. Before it does so, the Creuss player&rsquo;s other ships may move through the wormhole created by the <i>Hil Colish</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;or it can move after them. It can also use its own wormhole, for example to go home.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The delta wormhole moves with the <i>Hil Colish</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;Its system counts as containing a delta wormhole.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the <i>Hil Colish</i> moves before or after other ships, it does not generate a second <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> step.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If another player uses the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Light/Wave_Deflector"><i>Light/Wave Deflector</i></a> technology to move through a system that contains the Creuss player&rsquo;s ships, that player may move through the delta wormhole in the <i>Hil Colish</i>&rsquo;s system.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;&rsquo;Light/Wave Deflector&rsquo; allows a player other than the Ghosts of Creuss to move their fleet through the &lsquo;Hil Colish&rsquo;s&rsquo; system into the Creuss home system or the Creuss Gate system.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can other players use the Creuss Gate and the Creuss flagship&rsquo;s delta wormhole?&rdquo;: &ldquo;enemies need a way to move through it (such as Light/Wave Deflector).&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>During space combat involving the <i>Hil Colish</i>, either player may retreat to another system containing a delta wormhole, if that system meets the other requirements for retreating.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the <i>Hil Colish</i> is destroyed between the <b>Announce Retreats</b> step and the <b>Retreat</b> step, then the retreating player must retreat to a different eligible system. If no such system exists, then their retreat is canceled.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>When the <i>Hil Colish</i> retreats, it may retreat before or after the Creuss player&rsquo;s other ships, but cannot retreat in such a way that would prevent the other ships from retreating to the same system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <i>Hil Colish</i> is returned to the reinforcements by a gravity rift, its delta wormhole ceases to exist; other ships cannot use it to reach the active system.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;If the &lsquo;Hil Colish&rsquo; moves before other ships and is returned to reinforcements by a gravity rift, can other ships still use its delta wormhole &hellip;? A: No, the wormhole ceases to exist.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;If it moves first through a gravity rift and is destroyed, the wormhole is gone before the others move.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Hil Colish</i> is not a wormhole token. If it is in an entropic scar, its delta wormhole is unaffected by that entropic scar.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;What happens to the Hil Colish delta wormhole in the entropic scar? A: &hellip; there no effect from Entropic Scar on the Delta wormhole opened by Hil Colish.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The delta wormhole of the <i>Hil Colish</i> creates adjacency for the range of <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> abilities, such as <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/PDS#Upgraded_Unit:~:text=Deep%20Space%20Cannon"><sc>Deep Space Cannon</sc></a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. RulesPal (NOT USED, unconfirmed), &ldquo;Can Space Cannon with range reach through a wormhole?&rdquo;: &ldquo;wormhole adjacency counts for Space Cannon range, including the delta wormhole on the Creuss flagship&rdquo;.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="emissary-taivra"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Leaders:~:text=Emissary%20Taivra">Emissary Taivra</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Creuss player may use this ability to access the inactive wormhole nexus without a gamma wormhole. Moving ships into the wormhole nexus this way will cause it to flip.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do players reach the Wormhole Nexus, and can the Creuss agent help on the first turn?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the Creuss agent, used after activation and before movement, makes it adjacent to a delta wormhole system, so ships can move in that turn. Once a unit enters &hellip; the Nexus flips.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A delta wormhole in the system (such as from the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Flagship:~:text=Hil%20Colish"><i>Hil Colish</i></a>) does not prevent this ability from being usable.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook, Emissary Taivra: &ldquo;After any player activates a system that contains a non-delta wormhole.&rdquo; A delta wormhole does not stop the trigger.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If this ability is used, the active system will be adjacent to systems with delta and epsilon wormholes.<sup>8,9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook, Emissary Taivra card: &ldquo;that system is adjacent to all other systems that contain wormholes during this tactical action.&rdquo; All systems containing wormholes includes delta and epsilon.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Designer Q&amp;A, &ldquo;Using Wormholes&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Crimson Rebellion&rsquo;s &lsquo;Sundered&rsquo; ability says &lsquo;You cannot use wormholes other than epsilon wormholes.&rsquo;&rdquo; The ability names epsilon wormholes as a type of wormhole, so they are among the systems that contain wormholes.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a ship moves from the system containing the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Exploration#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Ion%20Storm">Ion Storm</a>, it will not flip, unless the active player may move ships through the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Exploration#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Ion%20Storm">Ion Storm</a> wormhole and chooses to do so.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When does the Ion Storm flip &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;With several wormhole routes, the moving player chooses which, if any, they use, which decides whether the Ion Storm flips.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The system must have a non&ndash;delta wormhole in it at the moment of activation.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook, Emissary Taivra: &ldquo;After any player activates a system that contains a non-delta wormhole.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If a wormhole is placed at the start of a player&rsquo;s turn in the system using the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Creuss%20IFF">Creuss IFF</a>, then Emissary Taivra may be used for the activation immediately following.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="sai-seravus"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Leaders:~:text=Sai%20Seravus">Sai Seravus</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The fighters are placed one at a time, until either one has been placed for each ship with capacity that moved through a wormhole, or the capacity of the system is reached.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When Sai Seravus is used, fighters are placed in the active system one at a time, up to the number of ships with capacity that moved through wormholes, or the capacity limit in the system is reached, whichever happens first.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The Creuss player cannot remove a ground force to create capacity for a fighter.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the Creuss player has a space dock in the active system, they may consider some of the fighters they place as held by the space dock, in order to continue placing fighters.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>This ability may be used whenever the Creuss player&rsquo;s ships move, not just during the movement step of a tactical action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the Creuss player retreats from a combat, then they will have no capacity in the active system, and so cannot place any fighters there.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player uses their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Leaders:~:text=Benediction"><i>Benediction</i></a> hero ability to move the Creuss player&rsquo;s ships, then the Creuss player may use this ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>A ship only triggers Sai Seravus if it moves through a wormhole, including a wormhole in the system it started its movement in. A ship that moves through a system containing a wormhole without using that wormhole does not trigger Sai Seravus.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Creuss commander trigger if my ship just passes through a wormhole system?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Only if the ship actually moved through the wormhole, whether it started in the wormhole&rsquo;s system or entered it along the way.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Systems containing Creuss wormhole tokens count toward the unlock condition of Sai Seravus.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Creuss wormhole tokens count for unlocking the Creuss commander?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; the tokens are wormholes for all purposes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="riftwalker-meian"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Leaders:~:text=Riftwalker%20Meian">Riftwalker Meian</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Leaders:~:text=Singularity%20Reactor">Singularity Reactor</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any units in either system are moved with their system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When the Creuss hero swaps two system tiles, do the units move with them?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; units are on the tile&rsquo;s planets and space area, so they go with it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any tokens on either system are moved with their system.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Creuss hero Singularity Reactor and tokens: &ldquo;All tokens stay with their original tile&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Systems that comprise The Fracture and the <a href="/F_rebellion">Rebellion</a> player&rsquo;s home system cannot be swapped with other system tiles.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook (Age of Exploration): &ldquo;New tiles cannot be placed off of the Ghosts of Creuss home system, the Crimson Rebellion home system, the Wormhole Nexus, or any Fracture tiles.&rdquo; Covers a different effect.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="icarus-drive"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Mech:~:text=Icarus%20Drive">Icarus Drive</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Icarus Drive does not have to be in the activated system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;For the Creuss mech&rsquo;s Icarus Drive, which system does &lsquo;this system&rsquo; mean?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The system the mech was in, not necessarily the one another player activated.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The wormhole token is placed in the system the Icarus Drive was in.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;a unit&rsquo;s &lsquo;this system&rsquo; always means its own system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="particle-synthesis"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Breakthrough:~:text=Particle%20Synthesis">Particle Synthesis</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Each wormhole in the system provides the <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> value and discount, even those of the same type.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Do multiple wormholes of the same type count separately for the Creuss breakthrough, Particle Synthesis? &hellip; A: Yes, each wormhole, even wormholes of the same type,&rdquo; provides it.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Creuss player moves the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Flagship:~:text=Hil%20Colish"><i>Hil Colish</i></a> into a system, the Creuss player may use the <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability of the associated delta wormhole during the production step of the same tactical action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Sarween_Tools"><i>Sarween Tools</i></a> applies when producing with a wormhole, as each wormhole has <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> &ldquo;as if it were a unit you control&rdquo;.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Twilight Imperium Wiki FAQ (not a numbered source), Ghosts of Creuss: &ldquo;Yes, Sarween Tools applies anytime the PRODUCTION keyword is present. Because the breakthrough grants PRODUCTION 1, Sarween applies.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ground forces produced this way may be placed in the space area or on any planet the Creuss player controls in that system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Twilight Imperium Wiki FAQ (not a numbered source), Ghosts of Creuss: &ldquo;When you produce in a system with an effect or with a unit in space, it can go in space or on any planet you control in that system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
